<meta type=article title="Minipage outbound references (#115)">
</meta>

<section #sec:intro | Introduction>

The document has a section and a figure that a minipage body can reference
outward, while the box's own labels stay sealed inside.

<fig #fig:doc src=doc.png | A document figure.>

<minipage #mp:out +numbered caption="A box that references the document" |
This box references the document figure <ref @fig:doc> and the introduction
<ref @sec:intro> — both resolve outward (read-through against the document
registry). It also references its own private figure <ref @fig:local>, which
resolves within the box.

<fig #fig:local src=local.png | A box-private figure.>
>

The document references the box itself <ref @mp:out>. But an inbound reference
to the box's private figure does NOT resolve — the read-through is one-way, so
the box's labels never merge up into the document registry: <ref @fig:local>.
